' =============================================================================
' FUJIBLAST for the ColecoVision on the FujiNet cartridge - in Amy.
'
' FujiBlast: a bomb-maze game for two to four players on FujiNet
' ("FUJIBLAST/FUJINET/2026"). This port follows the platform-neutral C client
' (c-ref/: main.c, net.c, move.c, play.c, menus.c, screens.c, test.c,
' appkey.c, game.h, proto.h) and the hand-written Z80 ColecoVision port
' (fujiblast-in/: the Adam port's screen, the Astrocade port's logic and link,
' M.U.L.E.'s ColecoVision cart layer). Amy port: Amy & Claude 2026, Amy
' Studio r12.12, optimizer profile balanced.
'
' The image: Amy's colecovision-fujinet target, a flat 32K cartridge (the
' program in $8000-$F7FF, the mailbox at $F800-$FFFF, the FUJI claim at
' $FCFC). Its RAM: the stock console's 1K, laid out as the asm port's
' ram.inc: ONE copy of the server's 247-byte state, patched in place as the
' frames come (no staged copy); the room list lives in it while no state
' does; the tiles to redraw are a bit each (MapD, 18 bytes) instead of a
' 143-byte drawn[] array.
'
' Controls: stick and either fire button; keypad * leaves a table (ESC),
' keypad # turns the sound off and on (M).
' =============================================================================
memory "colecovision-fujinet"

' ---- gfx.amy: generated by art.py (FUJIBLAST, Amy & Claude 2026) -- do not edit
' ORIGINAL PLACEHOLDER ART (the asm port's art was generated by tools not provided)
